WEBVTT

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.180
DRIFT

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.310
<i>Now, it's time for</i>
<i>today's featured product!</i>

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.440
Please don't touch my pudding.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.900
If you want it, please
ask for my permission.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:30.240
<i>An ultra-rare creature from Magmell,</i>
<i>the Seven-Colored Dove.</i>

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:34.750
<i>Believe it or not, this bird</i>
<i>possesses the remarkable ability</i>

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:37.000
<i>that neutralizes all sorts of poison!</i>

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.420
They live in the 45th Ward.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.670
Sir, you've seen them before?

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.130
Sure have.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:48.600
<i>Without further ado,</i>
<i>the starting bid price is...</i>

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.560
<i>one million esc!</i>

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:55.480
<i>Five million esc.</i>

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.360
Rich people really do exist.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.860
This is why people are
always getting lost.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.740
But it only creates
more jobs for you, sir.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:09.990
You'll be rich.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:17.210
It's oddly exciting to think how my job
thrives on other people's failures.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:18.960
Sir!

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.170
Amazing! Somebody bid a billion esc!

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.220
<i>Unbelievable!</i>

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.890
<i>The winning bid is the highest</i>
<i>in the show's history at one billion esc!</i>

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:31.810
<i>Congratulations!</i>

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.270
One billion esc, huh?

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:36.810
You can buy a pudding factory.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:40.360
Yeah, sure!

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.820
What are they trying to do,
paying so much money?

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.280
Shall we ask them?

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.430
A SEVEN COLOR PIGEON

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.140
Excuse me.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.180
Nice to meet you, Mr. Inyo.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.650
So you're quite the rich man.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.400
I ran an insurance company.

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:54.910
Then went on to security and tourism.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:57.030
How about a pudding factory?

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.240
Sorry to disappoint you, miss.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.160
But I don't have a pudding factory.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:06.670
If you do all that, I can see
how you'd bid a billion esc on a bird.

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:11.470
I can say my sole purpose of
working was to meet this bird.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.430
Mr. Inyo.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.470
I'd like to request your services.

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:26.980
I'm hoping you could find my friends.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.360
Where did they get lost?

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:30.980
The 45th Ward.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:35.160
So, they must've been poisoned.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.700
You're exactly right.

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:44.870
It's only common knowledge.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:48.590
The 45th Ward is known
for its poisonous inhabitants.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.710
Only fools would attempt
to explore that area.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.340
You're quite harsh.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:57.890
You guys are just naive.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.060
We were immigrants.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:08.360
Immigrants? It was a while ago
when immigrating to Magmell was allowed.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:14.820
Yes, my friends got lost 30 years ago.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:18.990
At that time,

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.950
<i>Magmell wasn't known to the world.</i>

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:28.210
<i>But because of that, the bond</i>
<i>fostered among immigrants was strong.</i>

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:33.760
<i>There was no way to survive</i>
<i>unless we helped each other out.</i>

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:40.430
<i>I was always with my</i>
<i>best friends, Stewa and Stein.</i>

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:43.430
<i>Everything we saw was fascinating.</i>

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:47.730
<i>Magmell was the perfect playground for us.</i>

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.190
I lost!

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:53.320
I won!

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.490
Man, you're too good!

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:56.650
Darn it!

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:02.740
I've got a brilliant idea!

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:04.370
What is it?

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:06.500
Tell us, Daysom!

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:11.000
Listen, we'll collect lots of
different kinds of bugs...

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:13.000
to determine the best!

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.430
<i>There were many poisonous</i>
<i>creatures in the 45th Ward</i>.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:23.390
I wanted to determine the strongest,

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:25.520
by making them kill each other.

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:27.020
Poisoning them.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:28.940
Yes...

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:35.900
At the time, I had no idea
we were doing such terrible things.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.400
What do you mean by poisoning?

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:44.910
You put poisonous bugs in the same
container and make them kill each other.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:51.040
The last one standing
is the bug with the most fatal poison.

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:53.210
It's an old charm.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:56.170
No! That's gross and horrifying!

00:06:57.010 --> 00:06:58.920
Yup, it's pretty sick.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:02.720
So, did they get poisoned by those bugs?

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:07.310
Yes.

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:10.940
I was the lucky one.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:17.480
But, I got scared so I escaped.

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:22.780
I kept my mouth shut.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:27.450
<i>I couldn't tell anyone that I left</i>
<i>my friends in danger and escaped.</i>

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:36.090
<i>The immigration plan failed</i>
<i>and we decided to leave.</i>

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:39.760
<i>We drifted apart from</i>
<i>Stewa and Stein's family.</i>

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:42.840
<i>We didn't keep in touch.</i>

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:51.140
I must've focused on working
in order to forget about them.

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:56.360
Before I knew it, I grew old
and accumulated some capital.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:58.900
So that explains that bird.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.950
Yes, I was set on obtaining this bird,
no matter the cost.

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:06.410
This bird that can neutralize
all kinds of poisons.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:10.700
Sir, I'm sure you know this,
but your friends are long--

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.290
Please don't say it!

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:17.630
Forgive me... I got emotional there.

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:22.670
This is my attempt to atone
for what happened.

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:27.550
By going back to where I left them...

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:33.560
To tell them, "It took long, but I'm back
to save you, I didn't run away from you"?

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:36.150
Yes, I won't deny that.

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:37.520
Shameless.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:40.940
I'm willing to pay any amount!

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:44.860
Please take me to them.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.910
<i>Hear that? He's willing to pay any amount!</i>

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:52.410
The rescue fee is 100,000 esc,
nothing less.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:56.290
But depending on my mood,
it could be more.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.130
Yes, that's fine with me.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:01.210
I may add more terms.

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:04.010
Whatever it takes.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.550
Great, then it's a deal.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:11.350
Thank you very much, Mr. Inyo.

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:14.350
Just call me Inyo. And...

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:17.230
you better find something else to wear.

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:20.360
Zero, help him out, will you?

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:22.320
Of course, sir.

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:16.120
So, how does it feel
being back in Magmell?

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:22.090
It's embarrassing. Compared to
my childhood, I'm very much out of shape.

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:26.670
But, it feels nostalgic to me.

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:30.930
Have you been doing this for a long time?

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:32.470
Yup.

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:37.810
I admire you. Saving others' lives
when you're so young.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:42.270
Mind you, I wouldn't save anyone
if I wasn't getting paid.

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:44.770
Plus, anyone can do this job.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:48.240
People just don't want to.

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:50.450
I see.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:52.280
Plus...

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:55.660
their rescue isn't guaranteed.

00:10:58.830 --> 00:10:59.830
<i>Sir!</i>

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:03.250
<i>There's sign of a monster</i>
<i>beyond this point.</i>

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:04.170
Got it.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:06.420
A... monster?

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:12.430
<i>It got picked up on the radar,</i>
<i>but I haven't been able to see anything.</i>

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:21.100
Stay there.

00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:27.820
In this area, know that
the more beautiful and innocuous...

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:31.860
the more toxic it is.

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:36.950
<i>Sir!</i>

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:45.920
Let's hope something hits.

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:54.430
That's...

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:58.720
A Chimeragift. They start out as
a tiny bug, but they transform

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:01.810
as they accumulate
victims they've poisoned and killed.

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:07.070
I smell trouble.

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:11.690
My eyes are spinning.

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:13.530
Inyo!

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:25.170
That deserves a medal.

00:12:25.710 --> 00:12:27.380
<i>Well done, sir!</i>

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:33.340
It's toxic to humans,

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:37.220
but a delicacy for a Seven-Colored Dove.

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:42.020
What's toxic and what's medicinal...

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:45.850
It's all about humans, isn't it?

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.670
<i>What are you doing, Stewa?</i>

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.500
<i>It's so we can find our way back!</i>

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:10.090
<i>You're so smart!</i>

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:12.880
<i>-Let's do it together!</i>
<i>-Yeah!</i>

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:15.880
Sir?

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:25.140
<i>Stewa!</i>

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:27.230
<i>Stein!</i>

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:39.530
In there?

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:40.830
Yes.

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:42.790
-Zero.
-<i>Yes.</i>

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:55.800
Look, Stewa!

00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:01.850
Quit that! This is mine.

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:03.600
That's a tiny one.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:06.430
Hey!

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:09.600
I found a bat!

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:11.400
Stein, that's impressive!

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:13.730
Man, that's a winner!

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:18.320
Who's gonna be the winner?

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:19.780
I bet the bat.

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:22.580
What? Then I bet the scorpion.

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:26.160
I forgot about that one. Darn!

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:30.920
Is it about time?

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:33.630
All right, let's open it.

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:39.340
<i>All because of this...</i>

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:41.840
<i>All because of this thing...</i>

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:45.770
<i>It's hot...</i>
<i>My body's getting really hot...</i>

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:50.520
<i>I can't see anything. It's all dark! Why?</i>

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:53.610
<i>Are you guys okay?</i>

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:57.240
<i>I... don't think... so...</i>

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:04.830
Bring them back! Bring them back to me!

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:08.660
Why... Why...

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.540
Why did I do such thing?

00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:14.920
Sir.

00:15:15.550 --> 00:15:16.380
Got it.

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:22.050
You're in luck.
Your friends are still alive.

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:23.930
Really?

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:34.770
There's something there.

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:38.230
Inyo!

00:15:57.040 --> 00:16:00.340
Yup, it's your friend.

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:05.550
But...

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:07.890
Stewa!

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:12.270
Stay there.

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:15.060
-Hey!
-Stewa!

00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:18.770
It's me! Stewa!

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:38.210
Stein?

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:43.340
Stein! Will you save me?

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:46.510
Of course not.

00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:58.940
It's Stewa vs. Stein.

00:17:00.650 --> 00:17:03.740
That's right! I could use this bird!

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:27.260
Jeez.

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:30.390
Let me handle this.

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:35.600
Wait! That's Stewa and Stein! Please!

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:37.730
Hey! Don't get in my way!

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:40.230
Inyo!

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:45.240
Stein...

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:51.160
I'm sorry I'm so late.

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:54.450
It must have been hard...

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:56.830
It must have been terrifying...

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:07.010
Stewa?

00:18:09.050 --> 00:18:09.890
Stein?

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:15.140
Do you guys recognize me?

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:23.650
Even when I've aged so much...

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:30.160
Inyo! It seems like they recognize me.

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:33.240
I'm so glad...

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:35.080
they're both...

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:39.870
I'm so glad they're both still alive.

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:42.540
Yes! Inyo.

00:18:44.130 --> 00:18:47.300
This bird will help
neutralize their poison, right?

00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:50.720
Yes. If you let them drink its blood.

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:53.720
Its blood?

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:57.060
But...

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:01.270
your friends will die.

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:03.980
But...

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:07.400
isn't it supposed to vanish the poison?

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:10.150
For humans, that is.

00:19:11.570 --> 00:19:13.820
The poison flowing in their blood

00:19:14.530 --> 00:19:17.910
is now necessary for them to live on.

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:24.420
Is there...

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:27.670
any way we could restore them?

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:37.680
They are...

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:40.310
no longer human.

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:40.620
Are you sure? Letting them die
is an act of kindness too.

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:43.660
No, I won't steal any more lives.

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:53.720
Even though they look different now,

00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:56.260
that's still Stewa and Stein.

00:20:57.390 --> 00:21:02.270
I myself look completely different as well
compared to back then.

00:21:15.030 --> 00:21:18.620
<i>I intend to use all profits</i>
<i>to conserve Magmell's environment</i>

00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:22.950
<i>and to aid those who</i>
<i>lost their loved ones there.</i>

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:26.960
<i>But why pudding?</i>

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:28.380
<i>Because...</i>

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:30.960
<i>that was an added condition.</i>

00:21:34.130 --> 00:21:36.550
You're allowed a maximum
of 20 puddings a day.

00:21:37.470 --> 00:21:38.300
Stingy!

00:23:11.020 --> 00:23:12.060
PREVIEW

00:23:12.150 --> 00:23:14.520
<i>Belena Stralia dedicated</i>
<i>herself to rebuilding</i>

00:23:15.020 --> 00:23:17.480
<i>an orphanage ridden</i>
<i>with financial difficulties.</i>

00:23:17.780 --> 00:23:21.530
<i>Fearless of all dangers she could face,</i>
<i>she headed to Magmell alone.</i>

00:23:21.610 --> 00:23:25.280
<i>She obtained many spoils of war</i>
<i>and miraculously returned home.</i>

00:23:26.330 --> 00:23:29.410
<i>Labeled as a miracle worker,</i>

00:23:29.750 --> 00:23:33.750
<i>people have been treating</i>
<i>her like a saint. But...</i>

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:35.290
<i>She's not a miracle worker.</i>

00:23:35.750 --> 00:23:36.590
<i>She's...</i>

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:39.970
<i>Next time, "Bloody Maria."</i>
<i>You should watch it.</i>

00:23:40.050 --> 00:23:41.880
Subtitle translation by Sachiko Takahashi
